cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Agentic Engineering: A Docs Template for AI Coding Agents"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-19"
authors:
  - family-names: "Diamant"
    given-names: "Nir"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NirDiamant/Agentic_Engineering"
url: "https://github.com/NirDiamant/Agentic_Engineering"
abstract: >-
  A copy-ready docs/ layer for AI coding agents: the files an agent reads
  before it writes code. Ships a lean root CLAUDE.md that wires the layer
  into context, templates for OVERVIEW.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, TECH_STACK.md,
  CONVENTIONS.md, DESIGN.md and HANDOFFS.md, and a running context log. The
  /apply command researches a real repository, plans the layer with the
  developer, writes it from the codebase, and has a separate evaluator
  agent verify the result against the files.
keywords:
  - agentic-engineering
  - spec-driven-development
  - context-engineering
  - claude-md
  - agents-md
  - ai-coding-agents
  - claude-code
  - developer-tools
  - templates
